micula ChangeLog
================

Version 1.1.2 (2026-10-29)
--------------------------

Bug-fix release. It corrects encoder output at qualities 5 to 11 and several
decoder faults found by testing against the reference `brotli` encoder and
decoder. Upgrading is recommended for anyone using encoder qualities 5 and
above. Streams written by earlier versions at those qualities may be invalid,
or may decode to the wrong bytes (see below), and should be regenerated.
Quality 0 to 4 output, the default quality 0 included, was not affected.

### Fixed

- Encoder, qualities 5 to 11: literal contexts were reset to zero at the start
  of every metablock instead of continuing from the last two bytes of the
  previous one. For input larger than one metablock (64 KiB by default) the
  first literals of each later metablock were encoded under the wrong context.
  Depending on the data, the stream decoded to the wrong bytes without any
  error, or lost sync and failed with errors such as "Copy length exceeds
  remaining MLEN" or "Invalid transform id". The reference decoder agreed with
  Micula's on both outcomes
  ([#15](https://github.com/cpkb-bluezoo/micula/issues/15),
  [#16](https://github.com/cpkb-bluezoo/micula/issues/16)).
- Decoder: a block-type switch whose block length was split across `receive()`
  calls was applied twice, so valid streams with block switches could fail or
  decode incorrectly depending on how the input was chunked
  ([#11](https://github.com/cpkb-bluezoo/micula/issues/11)).
- Decoder: with command events enabled (`needsCommands()`), valid streams whose
  insert lengths grew part-way through failed with `IllegalArgumentException`
  ([#12](https://github.com/cpkb-bluezoo/micula/issues/12)).
- Decoder: `close()` ignored bytes held back by the last `receive()`, so a
  valid stream whose final bytes arrived in a chunk of their own could fail
  with "Unexpected end of Brotli stream"
  ([#13](https://github.com/cpkb-bluezoo/micula/issues/13)).
- Decoder: streams with a window of 1 KiB or 2 KiB (WBITS 10 and 11) failed
  with `IllegalArgumentException` or could lose output, because content was
  batched, or a copy or uncompressed chunk emitted, in runs longer than the
  window. Windows of 4 KiB and above were unaffected
  ([#14](https://github.com/cpkb-bluezoo/micula/issues/14)).

### Tests

- Regression coverage for each issue, including a round trip with a metablock
  boundary forced every 2000 bytes at every quality, chunk-invariance on
  streams with block switches, and decoding at one-byte chunk sizes of a
  reference-encoded stream.

Version 1.1.1 (2026-10-29)
--------------------------

Security fix release for the decoder. Both issues affect malformed or
truncated input only; well-formed streams decode exactly as before.

### Fixed

- Decoder no longer emits more content than a metablock's MLEN when an insert
  length exceeds the bytes remaining in the metablock; such a command is now
  rejected with a `BrotliException`, and `insertAccum` is no longer sized from
  an unchecked insert length
  ([#9](https://github.com/cpkb-bluezoo/micula/issues/9)).
- Truncated input is no longer completed with zero bits. Reads and Huffman
  decodes that need bits past the end of the supplied input now fail, so
  `close()` throws on a stream that ends mid-symbol or mid-command instead of
  delivering bytes that were not in the compressed input
  ([#10](https://github.com/cpkb-bluezoo/micula/issues/10)).

### Tests

- Regression coverage for both issues, including rejection of every strict
  prefix of valid streams produced at qualities 0, 1, 5, 9 and 11.

Version 1.1.0 (2026-10-06)
--------------------------

Feature release: encoder qualities 0–11 are implemented end-to-end.

### Added

- Encoder qualities 3–11: deeper LZ77 search, static dictionary (identity and
  transforms), literal context maps, block splits, NPOSTFIX/NDIRECT tuning,
  larger metablocks, and Zopfli command selection (quality 10 one pass;
  quality 11 second pass with refined costs and shorter length samples).
- Google `brotli` CLI interop tests (micula encode, reference decode) for
  qualities 0–11.
- Ant JMH benchmarks for encode and decode throughput
  (`ant jmh`, `ant jmh-smoke`, `ant jmh-baseline`).

### Changed

- Relicensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License version 3.

### Performance

- Encode/decode speedups on the quality 0–2 paths retained from earlier work
  on this branch line.

Version 1.0.1 (2026-09-21)
--------------------------

Bug-fix release for Brotli encoding at quality 1 and 2. Decoding and
quality 0 are unchanged.

### Fixed

- Simple prefix codes (4 symbols): when the length-1 symbol was not first in
  sorted order, symbols could be written in the wrong order for tree-select 0
  ([#1](https://github.com/cpkb-bluezoo/micula/issues/1)).
- Insert-and-copy / distance: “copy at last distance” is only implicit for
  short insert/copy combinations; longer commands now emit an explicit
  distance when required by RFC 7932.
- Complex Huffman metadata: code-length trees are built as a balanced
  complete code (previously some symbol counts used invalid length-5 fillers).

### Tests

- Regression coverage for the reported reproducer, a certificate fragment,
  all four-symbol orderings, complex prefix codes, and seeded random
  round-trips at qualities 1 and 2.

Version 1.0.0 (2026-09-16)
--------------------------

Initial stable release of Micula, a pure-Java encoder and decoder for the
RFC 7932 Brotli compressed data format.

- Pure Java (no JNI); NIO-first (`ByteBuffer`); event-driven
  `receive` / handler API; incremental, chunk-invariant decoding.
- Encoder qualities 0–2 (uncompressed metablocks through LZ77 + Huffman).
- Maven Central and GitHub Packages coordinates `org.bluezoo:micula`.
- Requires JDK 21 or later.
